---
import GuideIndex from './GuideIndex.astro';
import MovementComparison from './MovementComparison.astro';
import Cadrin from '../layouts/Cadrin.astro';
import {catalogue,dateLabel} from '../lib/editorial';
import {localPath,term} from '../lib/i18n';
import {englishGuides} from '../data/english-guides';
import {englishWatches} from '../data/english-watches';
import {hasAffiliation} from '../data/destinations';
import WatchCard from './WatchCard.astro';
import WatchPhoto from './WatchPhoto.astro';
import Photo from './Photo.astro';
import CadrinMerchantLink from './CadrinMerchantLink.astro';
import InternationalNotice from './InternationalNotice.astro';
interface Props{kind:string;id:string}
const {kind,id}=Astro.props;
const {watches,guides,selections,finder}=await catalogue();
const watch=watches.find(w=>w.id===id);
const guide=guides.find(g=>g.id===id);
const selection=selections.find(s=>s.id===id);
const content=englishGuides[id];
const copy=englishWatches[id];
const selected=selection?selection.data.watches.map(key=>watches.find(w=>w.id===key)!):[];
const related=guide?guide.data.related.flatMap(key=>watches.filter(w=>w.id===key)):[];
const title=kind==='watch'&&watch?`${watch.data.brand} ${watch.data.name} ${watch.data.reference}`:kind==='guide'?content.title:kind==='selection'?'Three watches for everyday life':kind==='selections'?'The watch selections':kind==='guides'?'Guides to choosing well':'Our method and its limits';
const description=kind==='watch'?copy.note:kind==='guide'?content.description:kind==='selection'?'Mechanical, solar or digital: three ways to live with an everyday watch.':kind==='guides'?'Budget, proportions, movements and gifts: useful guides to finding a watch you will enjoy wearing.':kind==='selections'?'Short, documented selections that explain the differences without scores or rankings.':'How Cadrin separates published specifications, editorial interpretation and hands-on testing.';
const sourceLabel=(url:string,i:number)=>`${new URL(url).hostname.replace(/^www\./,'')} · source ${i+1}`;
---
<Cadrin title={title} description={description} article={kind==='guide'} verifiedAt={guide?.data.verifiedAt} crumbs={[{name:title,url:Astro.url.pathname}]}>
 <div class="container">
  <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/en/">Home</a><span>/</span>{kind==='watch'&&<><a href="/en/selections/">Selections</a><span>/</span></>}{kind==='guide'&&<><a href="/en/guides/">Guides</a><span>/</span></>}<span>{title}</span></nav>
  {kind==='watch'&&watch&&<>
   <header class="watch-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">Documented watch / {watch.data.brand}</span><h1>{watch.data.name}</h1><p class="reference">{watch.data.brand} · {watch.data.reference}</p><p class="lead">{copy.note}</p><div class="reading-meta"><span>Specifications reviewed on {dateLabel(watch.data.verifiedAt!,'en')}</span><span>No hands-on test</span></div></div><WatchPhoto src={watch.data.image} reference={watch.data.reference} approved={watch.data.rights==='approved'} detail/></header>
   <div class="watch-detail-layout"><article class="reading"><section><h2>The documented specifications</h2><dl class="facts">{watch.data.facts.map(f=><div><dt>{term(f.label,'en')}</dt><dd>{term(f.value,'en')}</dd></div>)}</dl><p class="chapter-source">Figures published by the cited sources, not measured by Cadrin.</p></section>{copy.sections.map(s=><section><h2>{s.title}</h2>{s.paragraphs.map(p=><p>{p}</p>)}</section>)}<section><h2>Sources and limits</h2><p>{copy.limit}</p><ul class="source-list">{watch.data.sources.map((s,i)=><li><a href={s.url}>{sourceLabel(s.url,i)} ↗</a></li>)}</ul><p>Suggested uses are editorial interpretations. We have not tested comfort, accuracy or resistance, and publish no product rating or customer review.</p><a href="/en/our-method/">Read our method</a></section>{finder.some(w=>w.id===id)&&<p><a class="text-link" href={`/en/watch-finder/?comparer=${id}`}>Compare this watch →</a></p>}<section><h2>Keep exploring</h2><ul class="source-list">{guides.filter(g=>g.data.related.includes(id)).map(g=><li><a href={localPath(`/guides/${g.id}/`,'en')}>{englishGuides[g.id].title}</a></li>)}</ul><a class="text-link" href="/en/selections/">← Back to the selections</a></section></article>
   <aside class="merchant-panel"><h2>Before the retailer</h2><p>{copy.limit}</p>{watch.data.price!=null&&watch.data.priceCheckedAt&&<p class="observed-price"><strong>{new Intl.NumberFormat('en-GB',{style:'currency',currency:'EUR'}).format(watch.data.price)}</strong><br/><small>Recorded on {dateLabel(watch.data.priceCheckedAt,'en')}, excluding delivery. Check the current total with the seller.</small></p>}<CadrinMerchantLink id={id}/><p class="small-note"><a href="/en/our-method/#affiliation">Affiliate disclosure</a></p></aside></div>
  </>}
  {kind==='guide'&&guide&&<>
   <header class="reading-heading"><span class="eyebrow">The Cadrin guides</span><h1>{content.title}</h1><p>{content.description}</p><div class="reading-meta">Documentary guide · No hands-on test · Facts reviewed {dateLabel(guide.data.verifiedAt!,'en')}</div></header>
   <div class="guide-layout"><nav class="toc" aria-label="In this guide"><span class="eyebrow">In this guide</span>{content.sections.map(s=><a href={`#${s.id}`}>{s.title}</a>)}{related.length>0&&<a href="#references">The watches</a>}<a href="#sources">Sources and limits</a></nav>
   <article class="reading">{id==='automatique-quartz-solaire'&&<section><MovementComparison/></section>}{id==='choisir-premiere-montre'&&<section class="summary-box"><span class="eyebrow">Before you choose</span><h2>A watch for the life you lead.</h2><ol><li>Set a budget you feel comfortable with.</li><li>Compare proportions, not just diameter.</li><li>Choose a movement that fits your routine.</li><li>Try it on if possible, then check the seller’s terms.</li></ol></section>}{content.sections.map(s=><section id={s.id}><h2>{s.title}</h2>{s.paragraphs.map(p=><p>{p}</p>)}{s.link&&<a class="text-link" href={s.link.url}>{s.link.label} →</a>}</section>)}
   {related.length>0&&<section id="references"><h2>The watches in this guide</h2><ul class="source-list">{related.map(w=><li><a href={`/en/watches/${w.id}/`}>{w.data.brand} {w.data.name} · {w.data.reference}</a></li>)}</ul><a class="button" href={`/en/watch-finder/?comparer=${related.filter(w=>finder.some(f=>f.id===w.id)).slice(0,3).map(w=>w.id).join(',')}#comparaison`}>{related.length>3?'Compare the first three models':'Compare these watches'} →</a></section>}
   {id==='choisir-premiere-montre'&&<section id="comparatif"><h2>Three movements, three routines.</h2><MovementComparison/></section>}<section id="sources"><h2>Sources and limits</h2><p>Specifications come from the sources below. Cadrin has not performed a hands-on test or measured performance. Some source documents are in French or German. Budget examples are dated observations or research ranges, never a guarantee of current price or availability.</p><ul class="source-list">{guide.data.sources.map((s,i)=><li><a href={s.url}>{sourceLabel(s.url,i)} ↗</a></li>)}</ul><a href="/en/our-method/">Read our method and affiliate disclosure</a><InternationalNotice/></section><div class="guide-end"><a class="button" href="/en/selections/">Explore the selections →</a><a class="text-link" href="/en/guides/">All guides</a></div></article></div>
  </>}
  {kind==='guides'&&<GuideIndex/>}
  {kind==='selections'&&<><header class="page-heading"><span class="eyebrow">Narrow the field</span><h1>Fewer watches.<br/>A clearer choice.</h1><p>Directions to explore, not a leaderboard. Every reference comes with its facts, sources and limits.</p>{finder.length>0&&<a class="text-link" href="/en/watch-finder/">Filter watches by budget and style →</a>}</header>{selections.map(s=><section class="editorial-index section"><Photo name="wrist" eager sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 45vw"/><div><span class="eyebrow">Selection / 01 · {s.data.watches.length} references</span><h2>Three watches for everyday life</h2><p>Mechanical, solar or digital: three ways to approach an everyday watch.</p><a class="text-link" href={localPath(`/selections/${s.id}/`,'en')}>Explore the three watches ↗</a></div></section>)}</>}
  {kind==='selection'&&selection&&<><header class="page-heading"><span class="eyebrow">Selection / 01</span><h1>Three watches.<br/>Three daily routines.</h1><p>{description}</p><p class="small-note">Specifications reviewed {dateLabel(selection.data.verifiedAt!,'en')} · No physical testing.</p></header><section class="section"><div class="selection-intro"><p>We bring these references together for their different movements and proportions. There is no ranking: comfort is something to judge on your own wrist.</p><aside><strong>What we compare</strong><p>Movement, dimensions and suggested uses. A specification cannot tell you how a watch will feel.</p></aside></div><div class="watch-grid">{selected.map(watch=><WatchCard watch={watch}/>)}</div><div class="selection-bottom"><div><h2>Compare before you click.</h2><p>Read each watch’s dimensions and the points to confirm with the retailer.</p><a class="button" href={`/en/watch-finder/?comparer=${selected.map(w=>w.id).join(',')}#comparaison`}>Compare the three watches →</a></div><div><h2>Still deciding?</h2><p>Return to four useful questions: budget, size, movement and everyday use.</p><a class="text-link" href="/en/guides/choosing-your-first-watch/">Read the first-watch guide →</a></div></div></section></>}
  {kind==='method'&&<><header class="reading-heading"><span class="eyebrow">Our agreement with readers</span><h1>A clear point of view.<br/>Clear limits, too.</h1><p>Cadrin helps you choose a watch. To be useful, a recommendation must explain what supports it and what still needs checking.</p></header><article class="reading method-page"><section><h2>Facts come first</h2><p>We prioritise manufacturer specifications and identify information supplied by a retailer. The exact reference and original source matter. Measurements from a similar variant do not document the model being discussed. The displayed date records our factual check, not a new physical test.</p></section><section><h2>Editorial interpretation, not a hands-on review</h2><p>Suggestions such as everyday or office wear interpret dimensions, movement and design. None of the watches in this version has been physically tested by Cadrin. We publish no measured accuracy, invented comfort impressions or product scores.</p><p>Diameter does not predict comfort. Lug-to-lug length, thickness, bracelet construction and your wrist also matter.</p></section><section><h2>Photographs in their proper place</h2><p>Our worn-watch images set a mood. Their captions say that they are not selected models. They do not depict the references we recommend. Photographs by Renzo Watches and Alex Boscarato are used under the <a href="https://unsplash.com/license">Unsplash licence</a>, with source credits beneath each image. Product photographs remain unavailable until reference matching and usage rights are documented.</p></section><section id="affiliation"><h2>Affiliation and transparency</h2><p>Cadrin’s intended business model is affiliate publishing: a purchase through a paid link could earn us a commission. That commercial interest should be visible to you.</p>{hasAffiliation?<p>Some links are affiliate links. Each paid link is identified near the recommendation.</p>:<p><strong>No affiliate links are active in this version.</strong> Our Tempus product links are ordinary links and earn no commission.</p>}<p>We do not rank watches by commission and do not promise the lowest price or available stock.</p></section><section><h2>Language and delivery are different questions</h2><p>English helps more readers use our guides. It does not mean the same shipping terms apply in every country. Tempus states that it ships worldwide; confirm the exact destination, delivery charges, any import charges and returns with the retailer. Prices here remain dated euro observations. Tempus may redirect its English product URLs or show partially translated pages.</p><InternationalNotice/></section><section><h2>Your browsing</h2><p>There is no reader account, newsletter form or third-party analytics. Filters run in your browser and their choices stay in the page URL. We save your explicit language choice on your device when storage is available. You can switch languages at any time. External websites apply their own rules.</p></section><a class="button" href="/en/selections/">Explore the selections →</a></article></>}
 </div>
</Cadrin>
